## **Bacanora**

终于，我们回到了Bacanora。

### **History of Bacanora**

[From article: 77 Years Outlawed, Sonora’s Rebel Spirit Lives: Bacanora—Spirit of Sonora’s Desert](https://theagavecompass.substack.com/p/77-years-outlawed-sonoras-rebel-spirit)

In 1915, the governor of Sonora, Plutarco Elías Calles (who later became president of Mexico), declared war on local distillers. He saw homemade spirits as backward, unregulated, and a threat to modernization. Officially, it was about control and taxation; unofficially, it was about consolidating power.

The punishment was severe: fines, destruction of stills, and even imprisonment. Local legend claims some producers were forced to smash their copper stills under government orders. Yet in the Sierra Madre and the rugged desert valleys, people adapted. They hid their remains in caves, roasted agave under camouflage, and used mule paths to transport their contraband.

For comparison: U.S. Prohibition lasted 13 years (1920–1933). Bacanora’s prohibition lasted 77 years. That makes it one of the most extended alcohol bans in modern history—and one of the most successfully defied.

When legalization finally came in 1992, it was less about permission and more about recognition of what had already endured. Bacanora hadn’t just survived the ban; it had become a badge of Sonoran identity—fiery, proud, and impossible to erase.

### **Mezcal, Tequila, Bacanora**

[Paper: BACANORA INDUSTRY AND ITS PROCESS OF PRODUCTION](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/241684661_INDUSTRIA_DEL_BACANORA_Y_SU_PROCESO_DE_ELABORACION_BACANORA_INDUSTRY_AND_ITS_PROCESS_OF_PRODUCTION)

> Sin embargo, con laintroducción de la técnica de destilación por los misionerosespañoles en el siglo XVI, las bebidas fermentadas sesustituyeron por los destilados de agave, los cuales, desdeentonces han evolucionado en diferentes productosdestacando entre ellos el tequila, el mezcal y el bacanora(Mc Vaugh, 1989)

在这个引用中可以看到，当时，Bacanora甚至是可以和Tequila, Mezcal齐名的一个产品，放在一起讨论。但是今天如果不是nerd，或许都不会知道Bacanora。

禁令持续了77年,使巴卡诺拉产业失去了与龙舌兰酒同步发展的机会。索诺拉就在美国边境上。在1915年禁令之前,巴卡诺拉是美国西南部的流行饮料。

历史证据表明,尽管这一活动在长达三百年的时间里遭受根除企图,但其持续存在不仅源于经济因素,更在于它在索诺拉山区人口最根深蒂固的文化和传统实践中所扮演的角色。[La industria del bacanora: historia y tradición de resistencia en la sierra sonorense](https://www.scielo.org.mx/scielo.php?script=sci_arttext&pid=S1870-39252007000200005).


Authority will ever win. 干杯吧朋友

